drenal glands are crucial for hormone regulation and can be implicated in various medical conditions.", "TUMORES NEUROENDOCRINOS PANCREÁTICOS:Los tumores neuroendocrinos pancreáticos son una causa de secreción ectópica de ACTH, que puede contribuir al síndrome de Cushing.", "CARCINOMAS DE CÉLULAS PEQUEÑAS PULMONARES:Los carcinomas de células pequeñas pulmonares pueden causar síndrome de Cushing por producción ectópica de ACTH.", "PROTEÍNA GSΑ:La proteína Gsα es una proteína reguladora que juega un papel crucial en la señalización celular y está implicada en la enfermedad de McCune-Albright.", "LITERATURA REVISADA:La literatura revisada se refiere a la información actualizada sobre el síndrome de Cushing, que se encuentra en fuentes como UpToDate.", "GLANDULAS SUPRARRENALES:Las glándulas suprarrenales son órganos que producen hormonas, incluyendo cortisol, y su crecimiento bilateral puede ser diagnóstico del síndrome de Cushing.", "MUTACIONES SOMÁTICAS:", "GLUCOCORTICOIDS:Glucocorticoids are a class of steroid hormones that play a significant role in the regulation of metabolism and immune response. However, when used long-term or excessively, glucocorticoids can lead to osteoporosis, a condition characterized by weakened bones. This adverse effect occurs due to their impact on calcium absorption and bone formation, making individuals more susceptible to bone density loss. Additionally, resistance to glucocorticoids can result in various clinical conditions, highlighting the importance of careful management of these medications.", "DEXAMETHASONE:Dexamethasone is a synthetic glucocorticoid and corticosteroid medication utilized in the diagnosis and treatment of various medical conditions. It is commonly employed in tests to suppress cortisol production, aiding in the diagnosis of conditions such as Cushing syndrome. Additionally, Dexamethasone is used to differentiate between functional and tumor-related causes of hyperandrogenism. Its therapeutic applications include the treatment of Cushing's syndrome, where it works to suppress adrenocorticotropic hormone (ACTH) levels. Overall, Dexamethasone plays a significant role in both diagnostic and therapeutic settings related to hormonal disorders."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}